	"id": "try-catch-gives-unknown",
	"text": "So how do you deal with exploding Promises? You wrap your code in a try/catch block. Tragically, the error you catch is always of type unknown, which is of little help. To handle it, you must pattern match, guided by what you've learned through your prior code spelunking. Alas, the type checker will not warn you if your assumptions were wrong, or if they change in the future.",
